Here are clearer, more consistent, and business-friendly descriptions for each column. I also corrected spelling, grammar, and standardized the terminology.

Column Name	Improved Description

long_person_id	Unique longitudinal person identifier used to track the same child across multiple referrals.
referral_id	System-generated referral identifier. Unique referral number assigned to each intake.
person_id	System-generated person identifier used to track an individual within a referral.
referral_type	Type of referral (e.g., GPS or CPS).
referral_received_date	Date the referral was received.
incident_begin_date	Date the reported incident began.
incident_end_date	Date the reported incident ended.
allegation_id	System-generated identifier used to uniquely track each allegation associated with a referral.
category_of_abuse	Primary category of the reported abuse or neglect allegation.
subcategory_of_abuse	Subcategory of the reported abuse or neglect allegation.
allegation_outcome	Final disposition or outcome of the allegation.
leading_lagging_indicator	Indicates the timing of the first subsequent CPS referral relative to the index GPS referral. The indicator compares the referral_received_date of the index GPS referral with the incident_begin_date of the first subsequent CPS referral. Values include:<br><br>• Lagging – The CPS incident began before the index GPS referral was received.<br>• Leading – The CPS incident began after the index GPS referral was received.<br>• Same Day – The CPS incident began on the same date the index GPS referral was received.
is_index	Derived flag indicating whether the referral is the child's first referral with a valid allegation (index referral).
subseq_CPS_referral_ind	Derived flag indicating whether the index referral has one or more subsequent CPS referrals with a valid allegation.


General improvements made

Standardized on "System-generated" instead of "System created."

Used "identifier" instead of "ID" where appropriate for documentation.

Standardized all date descriptions to begin with "Date...".

Used consistent language such as "derived flag," "unique identifier," and "subsequent referral."

Corrected spelling and grammar (e.g., received, classifies, indicates, subsequent).


These descriptions are suitable for a data dictionary or metadata documentation.
